<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95323" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκύλος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>animal's skin, hide</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δὲ ς. ἀνδρὶ καλύπτρη</span>, of
			a lion's skin, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				142
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.142
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.35
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				165
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Phal.
			</span></i>); <i>outer husk</i> of a nut, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				270
			</span></i>: heterocl. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκύλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					422
				</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκυλος</span> is 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῦτος</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				3.68
			</span></i>.</div>
